	(footprint "my-soffle:USB_C_Receptacle_HongCheng_HC-TYPE-C-16P_MidMount"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "1ee14515-dad9-4f50-9db2-db02416a2387")
		(at 168.779481 61.375)
		(descr "Hong Cheng HC-TYPE-C-16P-C16B (LCSC C19274022), mid-mount (sinking) USB-C 16P, USB 2.0. Body sinks 1.60 mm below the board top, so it is flush with the bottom of a 1.6 mm PCB. The origin is the mouth centre on the board edge, which is the ergogen usbc_* point the placement script puts it on. Needs a 9.24 x 5.75 mm cutout opening onto the board edge, shown here on F.Fab: it belongs to the board outline (ergogen _port_slots), because a notch drawn on a footprint's Edge.Cuts only T-joins the edge and KiCad rejects that as a malformed outline. Land pattern measured off the manufacturer drawing, https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C19274022.html . The C10B (C19274021) and C08B (C19274020) sink 1.00 and 0.80 mm and share this footprint exactly. Do not import the EasyEDA model for this part: it places the shell holes 11.25 mm apart instead of 10.79 and cuts the slot 6.40 deep instead of 5.75.")
		(tags "usb usb-c 2.0 mid-mount sinking")
